                    <note type="editorial">
                        <p>Hanger, George, fourth Baron Coleraine (1751–1824), army officer, writer and rake.
    Hanger was an associate of Tarleton and of the Prince of Wales. Godwin's contacts are
    mainly through Debrett and Lauderdale, but he also sees him with Montagu. </p>
                        <p>Hanger appears under 1795 in Godwin's 1796 lists, which fits with his entrance into the diary.</p>
